[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   Step 125 -- displaced-structure temporal characterization.
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   Steps 117-124 established that the post-2017 SBDB cohort carries a
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   unipolar, longitude-organized rotation structure centred near
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   (120, -40) -- 79 deg off the declared axis -- that the CODE
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   machinery does not see at the same sky.  The factorial audit
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   filed it as a cohort-private systematic.  That label is a
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   diagnosis, not a measurement: a genuine field feature and a
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   fitting systematic make different predictions about WHEN the
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   structure should appear.
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   Under TEP the proper-time field is dynamical -- it varies in
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   space and in time (Paper 0, screening ontology).  A comet's
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   transit slip records the field geometry at its own crossing
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   epoch, and the Sun traverses ~5.5 AU/yr of interstellar medium
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   between transit eras, so a real boundary feature produces a
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   slip amplitude that grades with the transit epoch of each
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   object.  A longitude-organized fitting systematic, by contrast,
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   grades with the observing/solution properties of the record --
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   arc length, observation count, fit vintage -- not with when the
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   comet crossed.  This step measures the displaced structure on
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   both axes of that discriminator.
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   T1  raw-field free-axis scan on the post-2017 primaries (no
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   residualization): recover the maximum in-minus-out cap-gap
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   axis and its extremeness over the trial grid.
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   T2  era x displaced-cap factorial: median drot for pre-2018 vs
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   post-2017 objects inside the same displaced cap -- does the
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   same sky region carry the structure in both eras?
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   T3  transit-epoch gradient: Spearman(drot, transit_year) inside
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   the displaced cap per era, with rank partials controlling
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   nobs, arc, boundary energy aa_back and encounter depth denc;
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   the same gradient on the unexplained proper-time channel.
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   A real temporal structure grades with crossing epoch and
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   survives the solution-quality controls.
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   T4  geometry-matched pairs: each post-2017 displaced-cap member
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   matched to its nearest pre-2018 cap members on (log q,
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   aa_back, log denc, i) -- if the elevation is a property of
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   transit geometry, matched pre-2018 objects carry it too; if
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   it persists unmatched, it is a property of the modern record.
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   T5  named-direction audit: separation of the displaced axis from
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   the CMB dipole apex/antapex (the scalar-field rest frame used
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   in the GNSS/EFA/LLR channels), the ISM inflow, the solar
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   apex, the galactic centre and poles, the ecliptic pole, the
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   declared and detached axes, and the pre-2018 record's own
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   private axis (340,-60); plus the cos(theta)/cos(2theta)
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   decomposition about the displaced axis.
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   T6  quality stratification inside the post-2017 displaced cap:
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   arc and nobs halves -- does the elevation persist where the
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   solutions are best determined?
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   T7  cross-fitter concordance: SBDB vs MPC CometEls elements for
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   the same objects -- if the structure were a JPL-only fitting
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   artefact, independent CometEls solutions would diverge.
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   T8  signature-morphology discriminator: the declared anomaly's
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   defining characters are rotation without energy exchange and
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   an inbound-weighted leg distribution.  Compares the displaced
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   elevation on daa, leg share and bound fraction -- classifies
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   whether the structure is the same signature at a rotated axis
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   or a different signature class.
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   T9  observable-carrier audit: the unexplained-slip observable is
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   a disagreement between independently fitted leg solutions --
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   it exists only in three-leg records.  Tabulates signature
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   presence by record structure (CODE/Warsaw/LPC vs SBDB
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   pre-2018/post-2017 and the same CODE-overlap comets re-fitted
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   under SBDB single solutions) -- tests whether the modern
[2026-09-21 15:14:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 125]   flatness is signal absence or absence of the carrier itself.
